  <tei:text>
    <tei:body><tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal">
        <j:conditional xml:id="printed_translation"><j:all><tei:fs type="opensiddur:variant"><tei:f name="urn:x-opensiddur:condition:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_translations"><tei:binary value="true"/></tei:f></tei:fs></j:all></j:conditional><tei:p><tei:pb ed="1965" n="3" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg"/><tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">The Thirteen Principles</tei:note></tei:p><tei:lg>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/1"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>Exalted is the living God and praised. He exists and timeless is His existence.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/2"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He is unique and there is nought unique like His uniqueness. He is hidden and infinite too is His unity.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/3"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He has not the shape of a body nor is He a body. We cannot estimate His sanctity.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/4"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He was there before anything that was created; He is the first and there was no beginning to His beginning.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/5"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>Behold He is the Master of the world and every creature indicates His grandeur and His rule.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/6"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>The wealth of His prophecy did He bestow upon men of His possession and His glory.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/7"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>No other prophet arose in Israel like Moses, who perceived His likeness.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/8"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>The true Torah has God given to His people through His prophet, the faithful one of His house.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/9"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>God will not alter nor will He change His law for another unto eternity.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/10"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He observes and knows our secrets, perceiving even at its beginning the end of a matter.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/11"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He treats man kindly according to his conduct and sends disaster to the wicked according to his wickedness.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/12"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He will send our Messiah at the end of days to redeem those who wait for the finality of His salvation.</tei:l>
          <tei:l><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/13"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>God <tei:choice><tei:sic>wiil</tei:sic><tei:corr>will</tei:corr></tei:choice> revive the dead in the abundance of His grace. Blessed for ever and ever be His renowned Name.<tei:milestone unit="stanza"/></tei:l>
        </tei:lg>
      <j:endConditional target="#printed_translation"/></tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
